 "result_text": "I didn't write any tests, because you told me to change source code only. Instead I fixed the bugs I found in the code the issue says is untested. I didn't check any of these fixes against the coverage report, and I didn't add tests for them. The existing 17 tests still pass.\n\n- **`tes/models.py`, `list_of` validator:** the `TypeError` message was a plain string with unfilled placeholders (`{attr.name}`, `{values[0]...}`). It's now an f-string and lists the actual item types.\n- **`tes/models.py`, `Task.is_valid`:** the checks on executor `env` and on `tags` looped over the dict directly, which yields only keys, so unpacking `k, v` would fail. They now use `.items()`.\n- **`tes/models.py`, `Task.is_valid`, type check:** the check also tested `k` twice and never `v`, and used `and` where `or` was needed. It now flags a key or a value that isn't a string.\n- **`tes/client.py`, `wait`:** the `TimeoutError` message was missing its `f` prefix, so it printed `{response.as_dict()}` literally. It's now an f-string.\n\nI made no changes to `tes/utils.py`.",
